---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Ashicore"
  description="Enterprise-grade operations software for small manufacturers. Ashicore connects inventory, batches, production, purchasing, sales orders, and fulfillment in one operating core."
  path="/"
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Serious software. Small-team ready.</p>
          <h1>
            Operations software<br />
            for small<br />
            manufacturers.
          </h1>
          <p class="hero-copy">
            Ashicore gives small manufacturers enterprise-grade operational
            control across inventory, batches, production, purchasing, sales
            orders, and fulfillment — without the complexity, bloat, or
            months-long rollout of traditional ERP.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button" href="/pricing">See pricing</a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="#operations">See how Ashicore works</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ops-plane core-plane" aria-label="Operating core workflow map">
          <div class="core-line line-demand"></div>
          <div class="core-line line-supply"></div>
          <div class="core-line line-inventory"></div>
          <div class="core-line line-production"></div>
          <div class="core-line line-fulfillment"></div>
          <div class="ops-core">
            <span>Ashicore</span>
            <strong>Operating Core</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="ops-node node-a">
            <strong>Demand</strong>
            <span>Sales orders &amp; customers</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ops-node node-b">
            <strong>Supply</strong>
            <span>Purchasing &amp; receiving</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ops-node node-c">
            <strong>Inventory</strong>
            <span>Lots, stock, commitments</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ops-node node-d">
            <strong>Production</strong>
            <span>Recipes, batches, yields</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ops-node node-e">
            <strong>Fulfillment</strong>
            <span>Commitments &amp; shipments</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section setup-section">
      <div class="section-inner setup-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Getting started</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">
            Up and running in <span class="title-accent">days</span>, not
            <span class="title-strike">months</span>.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="section-intro">
            Most ERP systems were built for companies with implementation teams,
            consultants, and months to spare. Ashicore is built for small
            businesses that need serious operational control without a giant
            rollout.
          </p>
          <p class="setup-note">
            Bring over the practical pieces you already run on — items,
            suppliers, recipes, inventory, orders, and batch records — and start
            with the workflow that matters first.
          </p>
          <div class="setup-points" aria-label="Implementation approach">
            <span>Start with your real workflow</span>
            <span>Import the data you already have</span>
            <span>Expand only when you need to</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="operations">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <p class="kicker">Operating models</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">What kind of operation are you running?</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Ashicore is built around how your business actually moves materials,
          stock, orders, and work — not generic industry templates.
        </p>

        <div class="operations-grid">
          <article class="op-card live">
            <header class="op-card-head">
              <span class="op-badge">Available now</span>
              <h3>Batch manufacturing</h3>
            </header>
            <p>
              For businesses that turn ingredients into finished products. Track
              recipes, lots, batches, yields, shortages, purchasing, production,
              and fulfillment in one operating core.
            </p>
            <p class="op-examples">
              Soil production, food and beverage, cosmetics, candles,
              supplements, fertilizer, compost, chemicals, animal feed, concrete
              and material blending.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="op-card soon">
            <header class="op-card-head">
              <span class="op-badge soon">Expanding next</span>
              <h3>Assembly manufacturing</h3>
            </header>
            <p>
              For teams that build products from parts. BOMs, components, work
              orders, purchasing, and production planning without spreadsheet
              chaos.
            </p>
            <p class="op-examples">
              Furniture, kits, equipment, fabricated goods, packaged products.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="op-card soon">
            <header class="op-card-head">
              <span class="op-badge soon">Expanding next</span>
              <h3>Inventory &amp; wholesale</h3>
            </header>
            <p>
              For businesses that buy, stock, allocate, and fulfill physical
              goods. Know what's available, promised, inbound, and ready to
              ship.
            </p>
            <p class="op-examples">
              Suppliers, distributors, wholesalers, parts businesses.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="op-card soon">
            <header class="op-card-head">
              <span class="op-badge soon">Expanding next</span>
              <h3>Hybrid product brands</h3>
            </header>
            <p>
              For brands that make some things, buy some things, and sell
              through multiple channels.
            </p>
            <p class="op-examples">
              Wholesale + DTC brands, Shopify sellers, local producers.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <p class="kicker">Built for operators</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Built for the messy middle of real operations.</h2>
        <div class="chips" aria-label="Core workflows">
          <span>Recipes &amp; BOMs</span>
          <span>Batch production</span>
          <span>Lot tracking</span>
          <span>Inventory allocation</span>
          <span>Purchasing</span>
          <span>Sales orders</span>
          <span>Partial fulfillment</span>
          <span>Accounting-ready workflows</span>
        </div>
        <p class="middle-copy">
          Small businesses usually choose between spreadsheets that are too
          fragile and ERP systems that are too heavy. Ashicore is built for the
          middle: serious operational control without unnecessary complexity.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="/pricing">See pricing</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
